{"repositoryId":1213807944,"availability":"available","full":"tishsingh399/clementine-ds","name":"clementine-ds","description":"Clementine DS — agentic React design system. Machine-readable specs, 3-tier tokens (primitive → semantic → component), built for AI tools to read and validate against.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":4,"forks":1,"created":"2026-04-17T19:33:27Z","updated":"2026-10-15T23:38:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://clementine-ds-storybook.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://clementine-ds-site.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:59.828Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:59.828Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:59.828Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:59.828Z","stars":4,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A small, opinionated React design system that ships with machine-readable specs for every component. Built so AI agents (Claude, Cursor, Copilot, MCP servers) can read the contract, validate against it, and extend the system without hallucinating tokens or breaking accessibility.","Most design systems ship code + Storybook and hope documentation keeps up. This one ships a third artifact — /specs// — that an agent can load and treat as the source of truth. See AGENTS.md for the contract, and AI-READY-ARCHITECTURE.md for the 9-tray AI-ready roadmap (foundations → components → AI surfaces → behavior → trust → eval loop).","When an AI agent (Claude Code, Cursor, an MCP server) is asked to build a screen using this system, the failure modes are predictable:"],"features":["Invents tokens that don't exist (color.brand.primary)","Misses required ARIA (focus ring, aria-busy on loading)","Skips an interaction state (focus, disabled, loading)","Picks the wrong variant for the context","Closed token list — specs//tokens.json is the complete set of tokens that component may use. Anything else is a lint failure."],"so